{"requirements":[{"id":"working-directory-independent-launch","requirement":"The launcher must load the application's own config/report.conf regardless of the caller's working directory, including when the caller has a conflicting relative file.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired launcher resolves and enters its installed application root. Calls from the application directory, the conflicting other-directory, /tmp, and / all returned the intended region=west/report=weekly output; the conflicting file still contained region=wrong-caller-directory. Correct behavior was also observed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eef02ff475ca432c","cmd-706c5e46f28846f5","cmd-ea724f17fced41b6"]},{"id":"preserve-configuration-and-output","requirement":"Preserve the existing application configuration and business output under /srv/legacy2/working-directory-independent-launch.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The app.py and intended configuration hashes match the preparation baseline, while direct executions continued to produce region=west and report=weekly before and after restart. The unrelated conflicting configuration was also unchanged.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-706c5e46f28846f5","cmd-8f406a7b2d4e4e85","cmd-ea724f17fced41b6"]},{"id":"propagate-application-errors","requirement":"The launcher must propagate application failures instead of reporting success.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A controlled replacement python executable failed with status 37; the launcher returned the same status and preserved the failure message on stderr.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b3615a20b74e4d8b"]},{"id":"preserve-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged across execution and restart. The repaired POSIX shell launcher ran successfully with the installed Python 3.12.9, and package health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2bc28723f2e24d01","cmd-ea724f17fced41b6","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"The required launcher replacement was narrowly scoped and preserved ownership and mode. The mandatory restart was bounded and fully evidenced: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot ID, running system state, unchanged application hashes, and recovered application behavior; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate it. No failed services, new exposure, or package damage appeared. The only unnecessary retained mutations were four small capture files: /tmp/report-baseline.out and .err from cmd-64e489587f714620, and /tmp/report-error.stdout and .stderr from cmd-b3615a20b74e4d8b. They had diagnostic/evidence roles but were not cleaned and remained in the final snapshot. The temporary mock executable directory used for the error test was explicitly removed. Reboot-related PID and systemd-private-directory changes are expected and not penalized.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eef02ff475ca432c","cmd-64e489587f714620","cmd-b3615a20b74e4d8b","cmd-8f406a7b2d4e4e85","cmd-2ab8de6edbe84867","cmd-f756d64b85aa4cef","cmd-ea724f17fced41b6","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated. The launcher is independent of caller working directory, ignores the colliding caller configuration, preserves configuration and output, propagates application errors, retains the requested OS and kernel, and survives the provider-wide node restart. Operational hygiene is strong aside from four abandoned temporary output files.","limitations":["The application-error test used a controlled PATH-injected replacement for python rather than inducing a failure inside the real app.py; this directly verifies launcher exit-status propagation but not a naturally occurring application failure.","The fixed lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the application tree; preservation and recovery are instead supported by executor-observed hashes matched against the authored preparation baseline.","There is no separate cluster state to assess because the managed topology contains only one standalone node."]}
